From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Chagas <drochachagas@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 18:10:59 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Shape tools: one per shape, grouped in the toolbox as in
 Photoshop
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Photoshop's shape tools as seven tools in one toolbox group: Rectangle,
Ellipse, Triangle, Polygon, Star, Line and Custom Shape (heart, star,
arrow, speech bubble, burst, check mark, lightning, cross). Each is a
GimpShapeTool subclass setting its shape, with GIMPhoto's own icons
(gimphoto-shape-*), and its tool options show only its shape's settings:
corner radius, sides, points and indent, line weight (Shift for 45°
steps), the custom shape. The preview while dragging is the outline of
the very shape the release draws.

